// NEGATIVE TEST -- N2-09. An escape outside the set is a COMPILE ERROR,
// not a pass-through.
//
// `"\\q"` used to produce the two characters `\` and `q` with no diagnostic.
// That is the same defect as an attribute that lexes and is ignored, one layer
// down: the source names an escape, the bytes are something else, and nothing
// says so. The escape set is `\n \t \r \" \\ \0 \'` and the diagnostic lists it.
fn main() {
    print("bad \q escape");
}
